00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:40.190
Chairman.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.300
We have reason to believe this accident
wasn't caused by an engine flaw,

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:46.370
but rather from a bomb
placed in the engine room.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:48.970
It's a conspiracy! A conspiracy
by a rival company!

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:50.840
I agree.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.210
To be safe, we'd better postpone
tomorrow's new route opening.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.140
Impossible!

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.810
But what if it gets targeted?!

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:00.110
Our company's image has already been
severely tarnished by the last two accidents!

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.280
The 3WA!

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.720
Hire the 3WA!

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:10.750
Do Lovely Angels
Prefer Chest Hair?

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.430
The Chief sounded furious.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:19.000
It's probably because we
put a hole in the tower.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.900
It was collateral damage.
It's not like we did it on purpose.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.970
If things were that simple, there wouldn't
be a need for the police or the 3WA.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:27.240
That's right.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:31.500
No wonder there's been an
onslaught of complaints.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.250
Still, they sure gave it a nice tilt, didn't they?

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:36.110
Chief, take a look.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:41.260
What kind of place is the 3WA? Tell me.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.160
Ah... Me, sir?

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:46.760
Officially known as the
World Welfare Works Association,

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.430
one might say it's an "organization
that takes care of all sorts of trouble."

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:53.600
Well then, are these
letters of appreciation? Well?!

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.470
Are they thanking us for what we've done?!

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:55.900
Well...
Are they thanking us for what we've done?!

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:56.430
Well...

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.000
You have my sympathies, sir.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:01.510
Sorry!

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.340
We didn't mean to... be late...

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.550
So, you're here.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:09.110
Regardless of what you've done, you always
enter my office saying the same thing.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.010
Knew it.
Knew it.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.620
It's because of that...

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.290
You have a mission.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:15.620
Huh?!
You have a mission.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:16.320
Huh?!

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.160
This time, there'll be three of you.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.490
Who's the third person?

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:19.900
It's me.
Who's the third person?

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:20.660
It's me.

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:29.730
I'm Nova Grave.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:33.740
Nova's an expert on corporate crimes.
He has seniority over you two.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.770
Pardon me for asking this,
but do you have chest hair?

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:40.850
That's an interesting question,
but what need is there for me to answer?

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:42.850
It's relatively important...

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:44.690
...'cause I don't like chest hair!

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:45.190
Let me warn you!
...'cause I don't like chest hair!

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.350
Let me warn you!

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:50.960
I wasn't the one who
recommended you for this mission.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:54.630
You have the computer to thank
for choosing you, after your last mess.

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:57.630
Um, we haven't been told
what our mission is yet.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:00.000
I'll explain. Come with me.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.240
Hey, Mister!

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:03.500
Get going!

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.980
It's just cruel...

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:12.150
That computer isn't programmed to
understand a superior's feelings at all.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.240
You have my sympathies, sir.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.750
We already know what this is about.
It's that luxury liner, right?

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.790
The one that's making its maiden voyage today.

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:21.850
We also know about the two accidents.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:27.260
They say those two Cosmo Plane Service
accidents were due to engine flaws.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.660
That's nothing but a rumor.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:30.270
Huh?!
Huh?!

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:36.330
I've already looked into it. Those rumors began
right after their new route was announced.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.210
But in all of Cosmo Plane
Service's two-hundred-year history,

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.540
not once have they had an accident
caused by engine issues.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.880
So, are you saying a rival company
caused those two accidents?

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:49.780
There are enough reasons to suspect that.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:54.520
It's definitely possible because they'd
benefit the most. It's Investigation 101, really.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.260
This mission will be quite risky.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:05:00.750
The two of you lack experience,
so you'll be following my orders. Got it?

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.130
What did he just say?!

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:04.970
Pretty annoying, huh?

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:08.070
Chest hair or not, I hate guys like him!

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.940
Now, now, calm down.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.670
It's best to let the elderly
keep their egos inflated.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.240
I see...

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:42.860
No wonder the rival companies
are feeling pressured.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:45.540
It's a nice job perk that
we get to ride on that ship.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:46.840
Look, look.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:48.480
I think we're about to get another earful.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:48.810
Huh?
I think we're about to get another earful.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:49.280
Huh?

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:50.740
He's calling us.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:57.890
So the engine in question has no flaws?

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:01.150
I'm certain of it. If it did,
we wouldn't let her fly.

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:10.530
The check-in window for Flight 807, departing
at 13:20 to Planet Samar, will soon be closing.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:16.100
Any passengers who have yet to check in
should proceed to Gate 8 immediately.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:22.540
The arrival of Flight 204, scheduled
at 14:50 from Planet Prezar...

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:49.460
Thank you for choosing Cosmo Plane
Service's Tenan Spacecraft I today.

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:56.510
This Tenan Spacecraft is equipped with
a wide variety of facilities for your enjoyment.

00:06:56.510 --> 00:07:00.780
So please relax, let all
your daily stress melt away,

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:04.180
and enjoy your glorious ten-day voyage
aboard our luxury liner, the Tenan Spacecraft.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:11.990
Just kidding!

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.490
What do you think?

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:16.930
You'd be hitting on me if you were a guy, right?

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.090
Why don't I get to dress up?!

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:20.870
This is boring!

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:24.430
It was Grave's decision, so take it up
with him if you have a problem.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:27.240
How did the ship check out?

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:31.750
There's no sign of a bomb
having been planted anywhere for now.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:35.010
I'll be checking the ship's exterior in an hour.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:39.750
You two keep an eye out for anyone
acting suspicious in the lobby area.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.060
So we pretend like we're passengers?

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.120
That's right.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:45.490
Also, be sure to check places
where men aren't allowed to enter.

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:52.490
When you say that, are you talking about
the women's powder rooms?

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:55.140
We can't be certain the culprit is a male.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:56.140
That's terrible!

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:57.110
Terrible?

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:59.700
Is that why we were assigned to this mission?

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:04.470
I merely gave the computer all the factors
necessary to accomplish this mission.

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:06.210
Are you dissatisfied?

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.680
We have our pride, you know!

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:13.180
That's right! We could pull this
mission off just fine by ourselves!

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:18.120
Just so you know, the word "pride" is used
by people who have done their jobs properly!

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:22.190
Got it? Good, now get to work.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:24.290
That cocky bastard!

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.420
I hate him, I hate him!

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:27.620
He's definitely gotta have chest hair!

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.880
We've kept the Engine Room locked.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:36.210
Good.
We've kept the Engine Room locked.

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:36.840
Good.

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:40.070
This is the Air Regulation Room.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.080
Ah, sir! Wait!

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:58.470
You're really going out there?

00:08:58.470 --> 00:08:58.900
Of course.
You're really going out there?

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:00.060
Of course.

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:04.600
It wouldn't be like us to simply
do what that old man tells us.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:05.830
I agree.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:07.810
Have you seen a pair of suspicious men?

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:08.710
No.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.380
Here he comes.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:13.050
Ah, you two!

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:16.750
"What are you doing?! Do what you were told!"
"What are you doing?! Do what you were told!"

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:17.880
Right?
Right?

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.590
Are you mocking me?

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:24.430
No, we're not! I'm the one most
qualified to check the ship's hull!

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:25.420
What?!

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:28.660
This is Grave. What is it?

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:28.930
A message from the airport.
This is Grave. What is it?

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:30.060
A message from the airport.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:33.900
Two passengers were attacked and
found unconscious in the airport restroom.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:36.300
Understood.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.640
Then, the two guys you were chasing...

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:39.240
Indeed.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:39.610
So they're working from the inside?
Indeed.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:41.370
So they're working from the inside?

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:44.070
Yeah, seems that way.

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.150
What now, sir?

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.880
Take care of things outside.
I'm counting on you.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:52.650
Roger!
Roger!

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:55.760
Something's fishy about those
guys that snuck onboard.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:59.320
I think so, too.
They could just be decoys.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:01.730
See you!

00:10:55.320 --> 00:11:00.020
This is hard work. Guess I can't complain
now though, 'specially after what I said.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:03.990
No way!

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:24.000
A bomb!

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:35.990
Glad I came out here after all. This should
make him rethink his old, outdated ways!

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:42.390
Oh no!

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:50.030
Nanmo! Come here!

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.730
Disable them, quick!

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:25.340
Nanmo, pick up the pace or I'll scrap you!

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:28.160
I need to call for backup.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:31.510
What is it?

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:32.740
It's an outside attack!

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:33.550
What?

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:33.780
There are three of them!
What?

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:34.480
There are three of them!

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:36.180
I'll send Yuri immediately!

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:38.890
So the two inside the ship are...

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:48.790
Yuri, launching now!

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:05.610
There are more of them! The ship is
under attack from both inside and out!

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:33.370
Shoot!

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:19.750
Why didn't you come help me?!
I was caught in an explosion!

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:20.760
An explosion?

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:24.090
You didn't feel it? If we don't hurry,
this entire ship is history!

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:25.630
Huh?!

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.560
On top of that, the old man
isn't answering my calls!

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:29.500
Mughi!

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:31.160
Make sure these guys don't get away!

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:35.730
Grave!

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:38.100
You're hurt!

00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:39.640
What about the others?

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.940
They just left for the hangar.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:44.000
The computer is in bad shape, too.

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:47.380
Yuri, I can't tell where this ship is headed.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:49.220
Isn't the controller working?

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:51.620
Worst case scenario, we could go boom.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.760
Then we have to evacuate everyone!

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:55.250
Nanmo! Run a check!

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:03.890
Hurry up and open the door!

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:06.900
All right, coming through.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.510
It's broken and won't open.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:11.300
Get back!

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:19.650
You need to get going, too.

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:20.010
Abandon ship? But that's...
You need to get going, too.

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:20.480
Abandon ship? But that's...

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:20.950
Abandon ship? But that's...
Leave the rest to us!

00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:22.440
Leave the rest to us!

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:24.650
Quickly! Please guide the passengers!

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:25.580
Understood.

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:33.460
This grandma's the last one.

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:33.630
Okay!
This grandma's the last one.

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:34.230
Okay!

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:34.360
Okay!
Excuse me, Miss. May I be of assistance?

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:37.000
Excuse me, Miss. May I be of assistance?

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.900
Sure! Here you go.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:40.730
All right, then.

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:41.430
Hey!

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:43.540
Grave!

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.340
Hurry up and get out of here too!

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:47.970
We can't do that!

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.580
You caught the culprits?

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:53.250
Yeah, but the three outside got away.

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:54.580
Don't worry.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.670
Stay still or your bleeding will get worse.

00:15:57.320 --> 00:16:00.340
O-Okay! We won't run,
so don't press down so hard!

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:09.600
"The ship is no longer in danger of exploding,
but it has now strayed off course by 0.01 degrees."

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:12.900
"If it continues along its current path,
it will crash into Dolmedo City."

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:13.770
This is bad.

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:14.170
Indeed.
This is bad.

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:14.570
Indeed.

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:20.970
Kei, we have another emergency!
The auto control isn't working!

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:24.350
That means we'll just have to do it manually!

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:25.280
How confident are you?

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:25.650
Well, it's my first time flying such a big ship.
How confident are you?

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:27.670
Well, it's my first time flying such a big ship.

00:16:27.850 --> 00:16:30.150
At any rate, contact Dolmedo Airport!

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:30.710
Okay!

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:32.950
This is Tenan I!

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:36.090
Control tower! Control tower, come in please!

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:38.530
This is the Dolmedo City Airport. Go ahead.

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:42.720
We have an incident! Our computer isn't
responding. Requesting guide signal!

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:46.270
Roger. Please receive on 104.

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:47.070
Roger!

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:49.170
The airport is adjacent to the city.

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:51.740
Please set the ship's course
to the left of the guide signal target.

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:52.540
Okay.

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:53.770
We've got it, Kei!

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:55.440
Standing by, ready!

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:57.100
Left! Further left!

00:16:57.980 --> 00:16:59.450
Nice, you're doing good!

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.420
Altitude 24,000!
One minute until atmospheric entry!

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:04.250
Put the reverse thrusters on standby!

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:08.260
Huh? The reverse thrusters are out, too?!

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:09.750
What?! Switch with me!

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:12.460
What's wrong?

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:13.930
The reverse thrusters are too weak!

00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:16.660
Abandon ship! Grab the
criminals and abandon ship!

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:19.060
And abort the mission?

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:21.330
Leave the rest to me!

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:24.970
What now?

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:27.240
We'll just have to ignite the boosters manually.

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:28.870
Yuri, do what you can here!

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:30.540
Nanmo, go help Kei!

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:36.380
If only I weren't injured...

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:37.220
Grave!

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:37.910
Wh...

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.420
What?

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:41.260
Please keep an eye on that monitor.

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:42.420
Ah, right.

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:47.830
I refuse to let these girls see me as weak!

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:49.320
Right! Back to the right!

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:57.540
It's terrible, Chief! The Dirty Pair!

00:17:57.540 --> 00:17:58.440
It's "Lovely Angels."

00:17:58.440 --> 00:17:59.240
Y-Yes, Sir!
It's "Lovely Angels."

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:03.380
Well, that Tenan I ship the Lovely Angels
are on is freefalling towards Dolmedo City!

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:04.000
What?!

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:10.070
Left! To the left!

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:12.080
Keep steady!

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:18.950
Kei, there's no time!
We're entering the atmosphere! Hurry!

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:20.280
I know!

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:23.330
At this rate, we'll become even more
infamous as the Dirty Pair!

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.230
Oh, shut up!
At this rate, we'll become even more
infamous as the Dirty Pair!

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:26.460
Nanmo, get back!

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:40.080
Entering the atmosphere!

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.050
No good! We still have two red lights!

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:46.580
Kei!

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:05.030
As a precaution, please evacuate
to Areas A or C immediately!

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:20.680
Ready, Nanmo?

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:31.070
She did it!

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:31.330
Yuri!
She did it!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:32.030
Yuri!

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:34.600
Great job! Now it's our turn!

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:35.800
How's our course?

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:37.230
Grave!

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.140
S-Straight.

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:17.710
C-Chief! Do you suppose
the Dirty Pair failed?!

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:19.330
It's "Lovely Angels!"

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:21.230
Yes, this is Gooley.

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:26.910
W-What did they say?!

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.810
The case is solved.

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:31.190
Thanks to those two.

00:21:31.190 --> 00:21:33.390
Ehh?! The Dirty Pair?

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:35.180
Lovely Angels!

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:43.530
Just as you suspected,
the rival company was behind it all.

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:46.770
I'm just glad the passengers were safe.

00:21:46.770 --> 00:21:48.960
Well, we'll be leaving you now.

00:21:49.170 --> 00:21:50.470
We'll leave the rest to you.

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:52.540
That should help you get better.

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:52.910
And one from me.
That should help you get better.

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:53.570
And one from me.

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:55.740
H-Hold on.

00:21:55.810 --> 00:21:56.900
What is it?

00:21:57.550 --> 00:21:59.880
N-No, it's nothing.

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:03.380
If we ever have the chance,

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:05.650
maybe we could work together again?

00:22:10.290 --> 00:22:12.990
That is... if it's all right with you.

00:22:15.930 --> 00:22:17.000
You pass!

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.370
What a nice guy!

00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:19.300
Yay!

00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:49.660
The mystery began after I fell asleep that time
Ano toki nemuri no ato ni okotta mistuerii

00:22:49.660 --> 00:22:56.370
I was guided by a voice from the future
Mirai kara kuru koe ni michibikareta no yo

00:22:56.370 --> 00:23:02.810
I passed through a distant, silvery time tunnel
Giniro haruka na taimu tonneru nukete

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:09.480
And met a wanderer with unclouded eyes
Deatta sunda me no samayoibito

00:23:09.750 --> 00:23:11.920
Space Fantasy

00:23:11.920 --> 00:23:16.160
I came all this way just to meet you
Anata ni ai ni kokomade kita no

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:18.390
Space Fantasy

00:23:18.390 --> 00:23:22.260
I came all this way just to meet you
Anata ni ai ni kokomade kita no

00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:28.740
Even if you were from another planet,
Tatoeba anata ga betsu no hoshi no hito demo

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:35.160
It wouldn't matter to me, because I've fallen in love
Watashi wa kamawanai aishita nara

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:39.010
Dirty, Stormy Destiny

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.750
Dirty, Stormy Destiny

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:48.090
Love is zero G...
Koi wa mujuuryoku...

00:23:59.930 --> 00:24:00.870
Sheesh!

00:24:01.070 --> 00:24:02.270
I'm tired.

00:24:02.270 --> 00:24:05.170
Jeez, this show has no principles.

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:08.210
Huh?

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:09.780
What are you watching, Yuri?

00:24:09.780 --> 00:24:10.610
This!

00:24:10.610 --> 00:24:12.010
Let me see...

00:24:16.480 --> 00:24:17.350
Next episode is...

00:24:17.350 --> 00:24:18.520
One, two!

00:24:18.520 --> 00:24:22.360
"Go Ahead, Fall In Love! Love Is Russian Roulette!"
